# CrossRev review attributes — the function-context drivers hunk shaping
# diffs under.
#
# `git diff -W` finds each change's enclosing function through the diff
# driver the path's `diff` attribute names. Git already recognises these
# languages by extension, so this file changes nothing on a stock setup;
# what it buys is independence from the operator's own git config. The
# shaping call passes this file as `core.attributesFile`, which replaces
# the user's global attributes — a `* -diff` or an experimental driver in
# `~/.config/git/attributes` cannot widen a hunk to the whole file or
# collapse one to nothing. Repository `.gitattributes` read from the base
# revision still apply on top: repository policy outranks these defaults.
#
# Only `diff=` pins appear here, and only names git has long carried as
# built-ins. A name an older git does not know falls back to the default
# text driver rather than failing, so a wider set stays safe. Nothing here
# touches text, eol, binary detection or filters: shaping reads content,
# never converts it (`--no-ext-diff --no-textconv` on every call).

*.ada diff=ada
*.c diff=cpp
*.h diff=cpp
*.cc diff=cpp
*.cpp diff=cpp
*.cs diff=csharp
*.css diff=css
*.ex diff=elixir
*.exs diff=elixir
*.f diff=fortran
*.f90 diff=fortran
*.go diff=golang
*.html diff=html
*.htm diff=html
*.java diff=java
*.m diff=objc
*.mm diff=objc
*.pas diff=pascal
*.pl diff=perl
*.pm diff=perl
*.php diff=php
*.py diff=python
*.rb diff=ruby
*.rs diff=rust
*.tex diff=tex
